 "short": "Heat into work",
 "lead": "Work turns into heat without limit, but heat turns into work only in part. The Carnot cycle, an ideal gas taken reversibly between a hot and a cold reservoir, sets how large that part can be; run backwards, the same cycle is a heat pump. The Stirling cycle is a second example.",
